{
  "summary": "This module implements two decision functions: `decideFromRegistry` (kernel verdict via the 6-layer graph) and `decideFireFromGraph` (graph-based fire assessment with policy and ledger). It bridges the registry, kernel, and fire systems, ensuring the bundler retains the kernel by using value imports.",
  "checkpoints": [
    {
      "focus": "Silent catch swallowing PolicyStore errors",
      "lines": "175-180",
      "why": "The catch block silently falls back to the seed policy set; if PolicyStore fails for a reason other than a missing file (e.g., corrupt JSON, permission error), the caller has no signal that the real policy was not loaded."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Side-effect mkdirSync inside decision function",
      "lines": "187",
      "why": "`fs.mkdirSync` can throw (e.g., read-only filesystem, unexpected permission), which would propagate as an unhandled exception from a function whose contract is to return a decision evidence object, not to manage filesystem layout."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Type assertion `as LayerId` after string-array membership check",
      "lines": "110, 133-139",
      "why": "Both `layerCertifications` and the layer mapping cast `f.consumer`/`c.id` to `LayerId` after a runtime string check; if the consumer ID list and `LAYER_IDS` ever diverge, the cast silently passes an invalid layer ID to the kernel."
    },
    {
      "focus": "FireLedger construction with database I/O in decision path",
      "lines": "188-189",
      "why": "Opening a SQLite database (with potential migration) is an I/O operation that can fail or block; this is inside `decideFireFromGraph` which callers may treat as a lightweight decision call, not a database-init routine."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Registry rebuilt on every call with no deduplication",
      "lines": "121",
      "why": "`buildRegistry(scopeRoot)` is called at the top of `decideFromRegistry` with no caching; if called repeatedly for the same scope (e.g., in a loop over targets), it may redundantly scan consumers and re-probe layers."
    }
  ]
}
```

