  "summary": "This file implements the GI-OMP extension factory, registering tools for graph-based code analysis (graph-probe, graph-query, aether-code-audit, gi-consumption, gi-decide) with extensive path confinement and audit logging to enforce security boundaries and prevent path traversal attacks.",
  "checkpoints": [
    {
      "focus": "Path Confinement Security",
      "lines": "100-220",
      "why": "The `confineTargetPath` and `ledgerDirConfined` functions implement critical security boundaries against path traversal attacks; any flaw could allow arbitrary filesystem access beyond the allowed roots."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Concurrency Safety",
      "lines": "50-60",
      "why": "The `populateLane` serialization pattern prevents race conditions during session store population, but the promise chaining (`populateLane.then(fn, fn)`) could silently swallow errors and block subsequent operations."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Graph-Query Verb Dispatch",
      "lines": "300-500",
      "why": "The large verb dispatch handles 13 different query types with complex delegation to typed-write and ripwire modules; error handling and result formatting inconsistencies could cause incorrect tool outputs or security bypasses."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Audit Tool Security",
      "lines": "500-600",
      "why": "The aether-code-audit tool creates temporary directories with `mkdtempSync` and performs extensive confinement checks, but the `settlementLedgerConfined` function could have race conditions or TOCTOU vulnerabilities."
    },
    {
      "focus": "Wipe Operation Safety",
      "lines": "250-280",
      "why": "The `graphProbeWipeAudited` function performs global wipe operations with audit logging; missing confinement checks or failed audit writes could result in data loss or unauditable destructive operations."
    }
  ]
}
